# --- Player_task13.events ---
# Task 13: Footstep sounds by material
#
# This file demonstrates all three Task 13 parts together:
#
#   Part A — `me is moving`            : true only while a move/goto/face is active
#   Part B — `when me touches <mat>`   : fires on enter-edge contact with a material
#   Part C — `play step sound "<mat>"` : plays the mapped clip, cooldown-gated (0.3s)
#
# ========================================================================
# SETUP — do these four steps in the editor (no C# needed):
#
#  1. Create a Physical Material: Content window → right-click → New →
#     Physics → Physical Material. Name it "Grass" and set its Tag to "Grass".
#     (Optional: repeat for other surfaces, e.g. "Stone", "Wood".)
#
#  2. Assign the material to your floor: select the floor actor → Collider
#     component → Material = Grass.
#
#  3. Import a step-sound clip into Content (e.g. "footstep.wav"). Clips are
#     referenced by name only — folder, extension, and case are ignored.
#
#  4. Map the material to the clip: select the player actor → EventSheet
#     component → Step Sound Map → add entry: Material = "Grass", Clip = "footstep".
#     (Add more entries for other surfaces: Material = "Stone", Clip = "stone_step", …)
#
# ========================================================================
# Walk on Grass → play the grass step sound (only while moving).
# Standing still produces nothing (`me is moving` is false).
# Switching floors mid-stride switches the sound on re-entry (enter-edge).

when me touches Grass and me is moving
  play step sound "Grass"

# Example additions for more surfaces — uncomment and edit to taste:
#   when me touches Stone and me is moving
#     play step sound "Stone"
#
#   when me touches Wood and me is moving
#     play step sound "Wood"
